}, {\"n_events\": 12, \"window\": [34302, 36101]}, {\"n_events\": 7, \"window\": [36102, 37901]}]}", "latency_ms": 12, "tokens_before": 33765, "tokens_after": 33765, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_07797dbf", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [798, 131, 389, 1747, 1932, 368], "window": [9102, 37901], "confidence": 0.62, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "798 and 131 are connected only when time is ignored, and only through the extreme hub 389 plus relays 1747/1932 (the alternative entry points 972 and 1877 into 131 have no incoming edges at all, and 798's other branches 45 and 132 are dead ends). The unique candidate route is a 4-hop chain 798->389->1747->1932->131, which under a 600-unit per-hop constraint must complete within 1800 units. 798's five sparse events and 131's eight events overlap with 1932's activity in essentially one coarse bin, so no plausible time-respecting, gap-bounded chain exists; the apparent link is driven by hub popularity and relay volume rather than by ordered timing."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structure of possible routes (798 \u2192 131):**\n- 798 has only 5 events in the whole 28,800-unit window; its *outgoing* neighbours are {45, 132, 389} (step_02, step_04).\n- 131's *incoming* neighbours are {368, 972, 1877, 1932} (step_05).\n- 972 and 1877 have **zero incoming** edges in the window (step_10, step_11) \u2014 they cannot relay anything, so those two entry points into 131 are dead.\n- 368's in-set = {934, 1450, 1923}; 1932's in-set = {435, 1440, 1450, 1747, 1916} (step_09, step_12).\n- 798's branches 45 (\u2192890, 1855) and 132 (\u2192583) are dead ends w.r.t. those relays (step_07, step_08).\n- The only candidate route is through the mega-hub 389 (72 out-neighbours, step_06), whose out-set intersects the relay sets only at 1747: **798 \u2192 389 \u2192 1747 \u2192 1932 \u2192 131**, a 4-hop chain requiring total span \u2264 1800 units.\n\n**Temporal feasibility:** 798's 5 events fall in bins ~[10.9k\u201312.7k], [21.7k\u201323.5k], [25.3k\u201327.1k], [32.5k\u201334.3k] (step_13). 131's 8 events fall in bins 1, 5, 6, 9, 10, 13 (step_14). 1932 is inactive in the 798-active bins except bins 10 and 14 (step_15), and 131 has no activity in bin 14. Only one 1800-unit-scale coincidence region even exists (\u224825.3k\u201327.1k), and it would require all four hops to align inside it \u2014 with 798 contributing at most one event there and 1932/131 one or two.\n\n**Confounder control:** the apparent connectivity is entirely an artefact of hub 389 (step_06) and of the heavy background traffic of relays 1440/1747/368 (step_16: 200+ events, vs. 5 for 798). Static reachability and hub popularity therefore explain the \"connection\" without any influence-carrying temporal chain.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_07797dbf\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [798, 131, 389, 1747, 1932, 368],\n  \"window\": [9102, 37901],\n  \"confidence\": 0.62,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"798 and 131 are connected only when time is ignored, and only through the extreme hub 389 plus relays 1747/1932 (the alternative entry points 972 and 1877 into 131 have no incoming edges at all, and 798's other branches 45 and 132 are dead ends). The unique candidate route is a 4-hop chain 798->389->1747->1932->131, which under a 600-unit per-hop constraint must complete within 1800 units. 798's five sparse events and 131's eight events overlap with 1932's activity in essentially one coarse bin, so no plausible time-respecting, gap-bounded chain exists; the apparent link is driven by hub popularity and relay volume rather than by ordered timing.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 43021, "total_output_tokens": 9367, "total_tokens": 52388, "total_latency_ms": 118036, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}